{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nComplete ADR 0098 for LLM execution after the command/store cutover. Many LLM operations currently call `LLMConfig.from_env()` independently, even though `LLMRuntime`, `ProviderSession`, gate config scoping, and snapshot composition already exist.\n\nThe goal is one behavior-bearing snapshot/context per public operation, not deletion of a legitimate top-level composition convenience. Ambient compatibility may remain only at an explicitly approved boundary and must delegate to the central composer.\n\n`emit_shadow_snapshot`/`_shadow` (the RP-04 S1 diagnostic shadow retained by ticket 3a08) has EIGHTEEN production call sites today, not just the five LLM ones: five in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` (LLM — the mcp.llm.* tools), eleven in `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` (three LLM workflow ops — `run_workflow`/`get_workflow_status`/`get_workflow_result` — plus eight NON-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops — `bridge_fsck`/`bridge_projects_list`/`bridge_projects_set`/`bridge_projects_remove`/`_bridge_run` (preview+sync)/`bridge_run`/`bridge_status`), and one in `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py::_emit_operation_shadow`. Deleting the shared `emit_shadow_snapshot`/`_shadow` functions (AC5) requires every one of these eighteen call sites to stop calling them first, so this ticket migrates ALL of them, not only the LLM ones — see Scope.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Derive a focused LLM config projection from the existing snapshot/schema/provenance; pair it with existing non-serializable `LLMRuntime`.\n- Thread that context through gate/workflow/runner entry points so subcalls inherit operation policy rather than re-resolving it.\n- Preserve ProviderSession/provider-native auth, budgets, cache/output/retry behavior, tracing, and secret exclusions.\n- Add consumer-level metamorphic tests covering multi-step runs and failure/retry paths.\n- Delete the shadow switch/function and migrated ambient-resolution branches after parity; tighten the existing ownership gate and documentation.\n\n**Call-site classification (resolves the ambiguity between LLM vs. non-LLM `_shadow` sites):**\n- LLM sites — bind the NEW `compose_and_bind_llm_config` (ticket ec44's own composer): the five `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` tool bodies (via the underlying `rebar.llm.review_code`/`verify_completion`/`review_plan`/`resign_plan_review`/`scan_epics_for_spec` entry points those tools call, so CLI/MCP/Python callers of the SAME entry point share one binding path) and `_lib_ops.py`'s `run_workflow`/`get_workflow_status`/`get_workflow_result`.\n- Non-LLM sites — bind the EXISTING general `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot` (ticket 3a08's already-landed, already-reviewed composer; no new machinery), completing the cutover 3a08 explicitly deferred for these two surfaces: `_lib_ops.py`'s eight bridge/reconciler-mapping ops, and the reconciler's own `_emit_operation_shadow` call in `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py::main`.\n- Once no production call site remains, `emit_shadow_snapshot`, `_shadow`, `shadow_enabled`, and `SHADOW_ENV` are deleted from `_operation_config.py`, and any re-export of `SHADOW_ENV`/`shadow_enabled` (e.g. `rebar/config.py`) is removed with them.\n\n**AC3 fail-fast vs. the general snapshot's fail-OPEN discipline (these are deliberately DIFFERENT contracts, not a conflict to inherit):** `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot` (the ticket-3a08 machinery reused verbatim for the non-LLM sites above) keeps ITS established fail-open swallow — an unparsable ambient config lets bridge/reconciler ops fall back to their pre-3a08 ambient resolution, exactly as already accepted for CLI/store operations. The NEW `compose_and_bind_llm_config` this ticket adds for the LLM sites does NOT inherit that swallow: `LLMConfig.from_env()`'s own `ConfigError`/credential/provider-resolution failures propagate uncaught through the new composer, so an LLM op with unresolvable auth fails before any external call (AC3) rather than silently degrading to unbound ambient resolution. The two composers are independent; only the LLM one is held to AC3's fail-fast bar.\n\n**Parity-verification artifact (the concrete check that must be green before shadow deletion):** `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llm_config_authoritative_binding.py` (new, mirroring ticket 3a08's `test_operation_snapshot_authoritative_binding.py`) asserts, through production entry points: (1) compose-once/reentrancy — `review_code`/`verify_completion`/`review_plan`/`scan_epics_for_spec`/`run_workflow` each bind exactly one `LLMConfig` and nested gate/workflow steps observe the identical instance (`is` identity, not just equality); (2) value parity — a fixed environment resolves to the SAME field values through the new bound path as `LLMConfig.from_env()` produced pre-cutover (a snapshot-style comparison over every `LLMConfig` field); (3) the metamorphic/failure-edge/secret-boundary cases from Testing below. This file (plus the existing focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow suites passing unchanged) is the \"parity\" gate AC5's deletion is conditioned on.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/_operation_config.py` — remove diagnostic shadow machinery (`emit_shadow_snapshot`, `_shadow`, `shadow_enabled`, `SHADOW_ENV`) after every call site below is migrated.\n- `src/rebar/llm/` (including `src/rebar/llm/config.py`'s `gate_config`/`resolve_gate_config` and a new LLM config-binding module) plus CLI/MCP LLM entry modules (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`) — derive and thread one snapshot/config/runtime context.\n- `src/rebar/_lib_ops.py` — migrate all eleven `_shadow(...)` call sites: the three LLM workflow ops onto the new LLM config binding, the eight non-LLM bridge/reconciler-mapping ops onto the existing general `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot`.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py` — migrate its one `emit_shadow_snapshot(surface=\"reconciler\")` call site onto the existing general `compose_and_bind_operation_snapshot`.\n- `src/rebar/config.py` — remove any `SHADOW_ENV`/`shadow_enabled` re-export once the underlying symbols are deleted.\n- Focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow tests and cross-surface contract tests, including the new `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_llm_config_authoritative_binding.py` parity/metamorphic/failure-edge suite named above.\n- `scripts/check_config_ownership.py`, `docs/config.md`, and `docs/architecture.md`.\n\n## Testing\n\nHappy path: CLI, MCP, and Python multi-step gates use one snapshot and preserve current provider/cache/retry/output behavior. Metamorphic edge: mutate every behavior-bearing LLM setting after composition and prove the active run is stable while the next observes it. Failure edges cover missing/conflicting auth, retries, fallback, workflow subcalls, and secret/non-secret boundary leakage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Each public CLI, MCP, and Python LLM/gate operation composes one snapshot/context; every subcall and workflow step receives its projection/runtime without rereading environment/files/CWD.\n- [ ] Mutating model/provider class, timeout, retry, cache, headers, tracing, or repository settings after composition cannot change an in-progress multi-step run; the next operation observes the mutation.\n- [ ] Explicit supplied config/snapshot stays authoritative, and missing/conflicting decision-bearing provider/auth composition fails before an external call without anonymous/cross-provider fallback.\n- [ ] `LLMRuntime` and `ProviderSession` remain the live-auth and provider-resource owners; no secret/live capability enters snapshot bytes, fingerprints, repr, logs, exceptions, or schemas.\n- [ ] `emit_shadow_snapshot`, its migration switch, diagnostic-only production call sites (LLM AND non-LLM — see Scope), and migrated below-boundary `LLMConfig.from_env` branches are deleted. Any retained `from_env` public composition wrapper delegates once to the central composer and is structurally allowlisted by exact symbol/rationale.\n- [ ] The ownership gate fails on synthetic direct/aliased ambient reloads and carries zero post-cutover legacy exceptions.\n- [ ] Consumer-level metamorphic tests plus focused LLM/provider/cache/fallback/workflow suites, default suite, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates pass; docs and ADR 0098 describe the authoritative state rather than shadow mode."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788079206621182001,"uuid":"ddfbab76-02f9-4b67-8c8e-3f115f8d4985"}